From 934d4c158bd2b9937a03e19ad8932a8d02fa6042 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.local>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:34:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] hotfix (phase 6.1): bump Next.js to patched 15.5.22, override
 postcss + sharp
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CI's npm audit step correctly failed on next@15.0.0 because that version
has 30+ CVEs against it including one critical (RCE in React flight
protocol).

Fix:
- Bump next from pinned '15.0.0' to '^15.5.22' (allows patches inside 15.x
  automatically going forward via dependabot)
- Add npm 'overrides' to force patched postcss@^8.5.23 and sharp@^0.35.3.
  Next.js itself still pins postcss@8.4.31 (vulnerable) and pulls in an
  older sharp; overrides force resolution to the patched versions.
- Regenerate package-lock.json from scratch under the new constraints

Verified:
- npm audit --audit-level=high → found 0 vulnerabilities
- npm audit (all levels) → found 0 vulnerabilities
- tsc --noEmit → clean
- next build → clean, all 19 routes still generate correctly
---
